# Generic words that must never become leak patterns: each one appears as a
# normal English / product / protocol token throughout the codebase, so a
# whole-tree replacement keyed on it would corrupt the source. One word per
# line; blanks and '#' lines are ignored. Names are matched whole
# (case-insensitive) by scripts/seed-leak-patterns.sh, which refuses to seed
# a name found here.
datawatch
localhost
claude
ollama
opencode
openai
goose
aider
gemini
shell
local
remote
node
peer
host
server
cluster
default
verdict
pi
test
example
gpu
